  === Complete Solutions

  #sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The emir was appointed by the caliph and could be deposed by him. The relationship was one of delegation under a superior authority, not of independent kingship.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Usman dan Fodio's movement overthrew the Hausa kings and established the caliphate. The Yoruba and Igbo were outside its military reach, and British rule came a century later.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Alkali judged under Sharia, the emir heard appeals, and the caliph was the final authority. The Resident belongs to the colonial period, and the other two are Yoruba or Igbo institutions.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Seven chiefs, with the Bashorun at their head. They advised the Alaafin and could reject him, which is why they are the classic Yoruba check on royal power.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The ofo was held by elders and priests as a symbol of truth and ancestral sanction. It carried moral authority rather than military or fiscal power.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Ibini Ukpabi. Ofo is a title symbol, Alaafin a Yoruba royal title, and Alkali a judge under Sharia.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Yoruba had Obas and councils, so the British could work through them, but their power was checked and the colonial administration had to adjust. The east is the case where no ruler existed.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The native authority collected taxes, maintained order and ran the Alkali courts, all under the Resident and the Governor. Its powers were broad but delegated.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The inquiry recommended clan and village councils as a more legitimate form of local authority. Emirs belonged to the north, and there was no elected parliament in the east at the time.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    1900. The charter had been granted in 1886, and 1914 is the amalgamation of the protectorates.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Three Lagos seats were contested by the NNDP, and one Calabar seat completed the elective element. The north had no elective seat.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Macaulay was president when the NCNC was formed in 1944, with Azikiwe as secretary; Azikiwe succeeded him after his death in 1946.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The AG was the western party, led by Awolowo. The NPC held the north, and the NCNC drew its strength from the east and the minorities.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The north argued that it was not ready and that a southern-dominated government would rule it. The motion was carried in the south and rejected in the north.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Michael Imoudu led the strike, which lasted over a month and showed the strength of organised labour. The other three were party leaders rather than trade unionists.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Enahoro moved the motion in the House of Representatives. It triggered the crisis that produced the 1954 Lyttleton Constitution.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Lagos was detached from the west and made a federal territory, which is one of the marks of the 1954 federal settlement.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Balewa became Prime Minister in 1957, three years before independence, and continued in office until 1966.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The AG won 73 seats and was excluded from the NPC–NCNC coalition, so Awolowo became Leader of the Opposition.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Southern Cameroons joined Cameroon, while the Northern Cameroons voted to remain in Nigeria. The two plebiscites settled the fate of the trust territories.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Weights and measures are exclusive, as are currency, defence and citizenship. Education and agriculture are concurrent, and chieftaincy is residual.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Health is concurrent, along with education, agriculture and electricity. Defence and currency are exclusive, and markets are residual.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Section 4(5) provides that the federal law prevails and the state law is void to the extent of the inconsistency.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The RMAFC recommends the formula; FAAC then allocates the Federation Account. The FCC polices appointments, the FIRS collects tax and the CBN manages money.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Commission monitors and enforces the federal character principle. Tax collection, elections and audit belong to the FIRS, INEC and the Auditor-General.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Nineteen states in 1976, up from twelve in 1967. Twenty-one came in 1987, thirty in 1991 and thirty-six in 1996.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The state house of assembly creates local governments; the National Assembly creates states; INEC delimits constituencies for elections.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Derivation follows the source, so the oil-producing states receive the 13 per cent share. Equality of states is a different principle in the formula.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Ironsi's Decree No. 34 unified the public service and abolished the regions, a centralising measure that deepened northern fears and contributed to the July counter-coup.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Gowon and Ojukwu met at Aburi in Ghana to settle the crisis over revenue and regional autonomy. The failure to implement it preceded the civil war.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The phrase was Gowon's policy of reconciliation after the civil war ended in January 1970, and it is the standard quotation attached to the end of the war.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Murtala's coup was bloodless: Gowon was at an OAU summit in Kampala, and the takeover was announced without widespread killing.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
